{
  "an8.54:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.54 ",
  "an8.54:0.2": "6. Gotamī ",
  "an8.54:0.3": "With Dīghajāṇu ",
  "an8.54:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Koliyans, where they have a town named Kakkarapatta. ",
  "an8.54:1.2": "Then Dīghajāṇu the Koliyan went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an8.54:1.3": "“Sir, we are laypeople who enjoy sensual pleasures and living at home with our children. We use sandalwood imported from Kāsi, we wear garlands, fragrance, and makeup, and we accept gold and currency. ",
  "an8.54:1.4": "May the Buddha please teach us the Dhamma in a way that leads to our welfare and happiness in this life and lives to come.” ",
  "an8.54:2.1": "“Byagghapajja, these four things lead to the welfare and happiness of a gentleman in this life. ",
  "an8.54:2.2": "What four? ",
  "an8.54:2.3": "Accomplishment in initiative, protection, good friendship, and balanced finances. ",
  "an8.54:2.4": "And what is accomplishment in initiative? ",
  "an8.54:2.5": "It’s when a gentleman earns a living by means such as ",
  "an8.54:2.6": "farming, trade, raising cattle, archery, government service, or one of the professions. ",
  "an8.54:2.7": "He understands how to go about these things in order to complete and organize the work. ",
  "an8.54:2.8": "This is called accomplishment in initiative. ",
  "an8.54:3.1": "And what is accomplishment in protection? ",
  "an8.54:3.2": "It’s when a gentleman owns legitimate wealth that h